## Everyday commands
- `hyperrouter chat` is a full chat client; `/help` lists its commands.
- `hyperrouter usage` shows requests, tokens, latency and remaining quota.
- `hyperrouter settings` shows configuration; `settings set <key> <value>` edits it.
- `hyperrouter catalog --available` lists every routable free model.
- `hyperrouter sources` lists where the catalog came from.
- `hyperrouter skills list` shows Agent Skills; add one with `--skill <name>`.
- `hyperrouter mcp tools <server>` calls MCP tools; `mcp add-rea` adds REA.
- `hyperrouter agents` shows which agent CLIs can be driven headlessly.
- `hyperrouter doctor` checks catalog, accounts, service and client wiring.

## Authentication
The local router key is generated automatically by `hyperrouter setup all` or
`hyperrouter keys generate`. It is stored in the OS keyring when available and
exported as `HYPERROUTER_API_KEY` by your shell profile. `hyperrouter keys show`
prints it; `hyperrouter keys rotate` replaces it and rewires every client.

Provider API keys are separate. `hyperrouter providers --template --missing`
prints a shell template for the providers that still need credentials. Fill in
only the accounts you actually have; never commit that file. After exporting
them, restart the router service so it sees the new environment:
`hyperrouter service restart`.

